# Quinsy Studio — Agent Rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [.quinsy-studio/process/agent-context.md](../../.quinsy-studio/process/agent-context.md).

## Session start

```bash
./studio install && ./studio verify-worlds && ./studio focus <project> && ./studio execute <project>
```

Do the `NEXT` command, then `./studio execute` again, until `ACTION` is `HITL`. Do not ask to continue mid-sprint. `./studio resume` is a checklist; **execute** is the driver.

Active project: `.quinsy-studio/.active-project.json`

**Fresh clone:** run `./studio install` once (installs `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `@headlessui/react` for studio-library). `node_modules/` is gitignored.

## Two worlds — never mix

- **Studio HQ** (this repo): `.quinsy-studio/`, LO-* backlog — commit here only for studio work
- **Project**: `projects/<name>/` — **separate git repo**; never `git add projects/` from studio root. Existing apps: `./studio adopt` (do not `init` over source).

## Before implementing anything

```bash
./studio guard <project> "<user request>"
```

- `NEEDS_TICKET` → create ticket first, no code
- `PRE_IMPL` → gates 0–2 not done; run `./studio resume`
- `STUDIO_META` → only `.quinsy-studio/`, not project files

## Library-first (before any implementation)

```bash
./studio library list
./studio library suggest <project> "auth billing"
./studio library pull <project> auth billing button
```

Adapt pulled code in the project. After ticket done, promote if generic:

```bash
./studio library promote <project> packages/billing --ticket <ID> [--force]
```

## Sprint HITL (after milestone roadmap)

Autonomous mid-sprint execution; human at **sprint scope approval** and **sprint review**. Milestone review when all M* tickets done. Ideas: `./studio feedback` → `clarify` → `ticket --from-feedback`. **Never implement feedback during review.** When sprint tickets are done: `./studio review` → human `--approve` → **reuse review** (auto-harvest) → retro `--complete` (auto-harvest) → `./studio execute` `STUDIO_LO` immediately.

## Drift recovery

User: "back on track" / "resume project" → `./studio focus <p>` then `./studio execute <p>` (do NEXT until HITL).

## Library (gate 2)

Design approval promotes base UI to `studio-library/` (tokens, components, sticker sheet). Project styling stays in project tokens.

## UI design HITL (post gate 2)

Design-track tickets (`ui-new-component`, `ui-composition`, `marketing-page`, `workflow-explainer`): Team 10 spec with **in-context mocks** (§2c) → `./studio approve-design <p> <ID>` → Team 01 implement. New components in studio-library first (`component-creation-playbook.md`).
